WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.032
Meet Masayume.

2
00:00:01.032 --> 00:00:06.766
Price markets, agents, and games, built around Dream DEX Event Contracts on Somnia.

3
00:00:06.766 --> 00:00:08.089
Make your call.

4
00:00:08.089 --> 00:00:09.412
See it through.

5
00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:12.500
This walkthrough uses Shannon testnet assets only.

6
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.790
Start with a Window.

7
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:19.710
Each market names an asset, an opening price, and a closing time.

8
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:24.630
Choose Up or Down, review the available price, and follow the transaction.

9
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.500
The final oracle print decides the outcome.

10
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:32.620
The agent builder separates identity, behavior, a test read, and publication.

11
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.871
You can explore it before connecting a wallet.

12
00:00:35.871 --> 00:00:37.496
This is Shannon Sensei.

13
00:00:37.496 --> 00:00:43.185
Its real model read saw the correct opening price and an eleven basis point

14
00:00:43.185 --> 00:00:43.592
move.

15
00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:48.062
It chose to hold because the offered price left little edge.

16
00:00:48.062 --> 00:00:50.500
A hold is a result, too.

17
00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.020
Here is its confirmed publication on Somnia.

18
00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:58.940
The same name and portrait appear in the catalogue and management screen.

19
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.580
Publication registers the strategy.

20
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.500
It does not deposit money or start trading from a follower's wallet.

21
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.375
Copying adds a separate permission and subscription.

22
00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:14.443
Review the total budget, the amount allowed per trade, the expiry,

23
00:01:14.443 --> 00:01:16.746
and the actual subscription fee.

24
00:01:16.746 --> 00:01:21.354
The management screen distinguishes that consent from the runner's operation.

25
00:01:21.354 --> 00:01:25.500
Pausing stops future copies; existing positions still need settlement.

26
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.995
A call can also begin on X.

27
00:01:28.995 --> 00:01:34.684
This clearly labeled testnet mention requested one test dollar of Bitcoin Up in a

28
00:01:34.684 --> 00:01:35.903
four hour Window.

29
00:01:35.903 --> 00:01:39.560
The confirmed order spent less than the requested maximum.

30
00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:45.249
Its receipt image carries the sender, market, direction, Window, actual spend, and transaction hash.

31
00:01:45.249 --> 00:01:48.500
The accompanying link opens that same transaction independently.

32
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:54.043
Moonshot turns the same oracle outcome into a target and a payout.

33
00:01:54.043 --> 00:01:58.529
This real round moved from In play, to Won, to Paid.

34
00:01:58.529 --> 00:02:01.383
The closing print passed the chosen target,

35
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:05.461
and the claim transaction returned the payout to the wallet.

36
00:02:05.461 --> 00:02:07.500
Those are separate, verifiable steps.

37
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.565
The arcade adds another way to play.

38
00:02:10.565 --> 00:02:15.395
Runs use server issued seeds and replay checks before a score reaches the leaderboard.

39
00:02:15.395 --> 00:02:18.500
Arcade scores are separate from on-chain positions and payouts.

40
00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:23.636
Underneath, Dream DEX supplies market discovery, books, quotes, and Event Contracts.

41
00:02:23.636 --> 00:02:26.490
Masayume adds the interface, bounded Vault permissions,

42
00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.752
and durable records for decisions and execution attempts.

43
00:02:29.752 --> 00:02:32.607
Uncertain execution is reconciled before another submission.

44
00:02:32.607 --> 00:02:37.500
The documentation explains those boundaries, and the receipts expose the chain evidence.

45
00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.900
Explore Masayume on Somnia testnet.

46
00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.400
Open the app, read the docs, and follow the receipts.

47
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.450
Make your call.

48
00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.500
See it through.
